  "description": "issue #677 (SP5): per-turtle shape state is isolated. :a becomes an `arrow` and :b a `circle` via scoped `ask`; a single `stamp` under `tell [ :a :b ]` then emits one `stamp` per turtle capturing THAT turtle's own current shape (arrow for id 1, circle for id 2) — proving stamp reads per-turtle shape, not one shared value (spec/turtles-and-sprites.md's \"Shapes and sprites\": `stamp` draws the current shape onto the shared surface). Every change of the addressed set — here from `ask`/`tell` — also emits the addressing `primitive` event carrying `addressing: { addressed_turtle_ids, current_turtle_id }`, so a consumer can identify the addressed turtle set (issue #766, spec/rendering.md:193); `ask`/`each` emit one again when the previous set is restored, on every exit path.",
